  pages={178-183},
  abstract={PCOS is a widespread endocrine disorder associated with female reproductive age and, in most cases, results in the inability to conceive and abnormal metabolism. The unclear symptoms and the dependence of subjective clinical evaluations make diagnosis to be hard. This paper will introduce the idea of an AI-based system that merges numerical medical charts and ultrasound imagery in order to advance the degree of medical diagnosis effectiveness and reliability. The FLFPCOSDet model merges numerical data (e.g. hormone data, symptoms) that are structured with unstructured ultrasound images into a cohesive diagnostic procedure. Machine learning is used to process numerical data and the deep learning technique is applied to analyze images, but predictions are combined. The preliminary outcomes indicate a higher diagnostic quality as compared to classic techniques, which put forward the potential of both data types in combination. The proposed FLFPCOSDet model obtained an Accuracy and $F 1$ score of 81.5 % and 65.5 % respectively. Nonetheless, additional validation on bigger, diverse data is warranted, future endeavors ought to involve the development of the model, testing on wider applications.},
